msgid "Decision rules as a DMN model"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A DMN model is an open standard for visual and semantic execution of "
"declarative logic; DMN allows you to externalise decision logic into "
"reusable pieces that can be easily used in declarative way. There are "
"multiple ways of writing rules other than DMN, like: decision tables, "
"decision trees, rules, etc."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For this example we focus on using the https://drools.org/learn/dmn.html[DMN "
"(Decision Model and Notation)] open standard to describe the decision rules."
msgstr ""

msgid "Solution"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We recommend that you follow the instructions in the next sections and "
"create the application step by step.\n"
"However, you can go right to the complete example."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Clone the Git repository: `git clone {quickstarts-clone-url}`, or download "
"an {quickstarts-archive-url}[archive]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The solution is located in the `kogito-dmn-quickstart` {quickstarts-tree-"
"url}/kogito-dmn-quickstart[directory]."
msgstr ""

